  "asr_text": "But a separate autumn survey of people planning domestic trips found a much shorter plan. The average stay was 1.8 nights, with a median of two nights. These are different questions, but they point to the same unresolved tension. The wish for a slower experience is clearer than any broad move toward longer stays. Japan’s 2025 tourism white paper also says the country needs more trips per person and longer stays. That wording matters. Official policy still treats longer stays as work to do, not as a completed change. The surveys should not be read as proof that sightseeing has already been replaced. For now, the preference is clear, but the stay-length data does not show the same shift.",
